---
import DocsLayout from '@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout>
  <h1>Usage</h1>
  <p>Once you have installed Yora Academy, you can start using it by following these instructions.</p>

  <h2>Running the Application</h2>
  <p>After starting the development server with <code>npm run dev</code>, open your browser and navigate to <code>http://localhost:4321</code>. You should see the welcome page.</p>

  <h2>Available Scripts</h2>
  <pre class="bg-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-100 dark:text-gray-200 p-4 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto">
<code>
npm run dev      # Start development server
npm run build    # Build for production
npm run preview  # Preview production build</code></pre>

  <h2>Configuration</h2>
  <p>The main configuration file is <code>astro.config.mjs</code>. Here you can customize site settings, integrations, and output formats.</p>

  <h2>Deployment</h2>
  <p>To deploy your documentation site, run the build command and upload the <code>dist</code> folder to your hosting provider.</p>
  <pre class="bg-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-100 dark:text-gray-200 p-4 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto"><code>npm run build</code></pre>

  <h2>Laravel Integration Example</h2>
  <p>Here's a sample Laravel controller integration:</p>

  <pre class="bg-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-100 dark:text-gray-200 p-4 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto"><code>
&lt;?php

namespace App\Http\Controllers;

use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use App\Models\Course;

class CourseController extends Controller
&#123;
    public function index()
    &#123;
        $courses = Course::all();
        return view('courses.index', compact('courses'));
    &#125;

    public function show($id)
    &#123;
        $course = Course::findOrFail($id);
        return view('courses.show', compact('course'));
    &#125;
&#125;
  </code></pre>

  <h2>API Usage</h2>
  <p>You can interact with the API using the following endpoints:</p>
  <pre class="bg-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-100 dark:text-gray-200 p-4 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto"><code>GET /api/courses
POST /api/courses
GET /api/courses/:id
PUT /api/courses/:id
DELETE /api/courses/:id</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>